From f4481efdbd154cc83cd18fae8e5cee57f5d56b79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blame42 <346530647+git-blame-42@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:26:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Add Route::resource and Route::prefix to the router

Route::resource registers the 8 RESTful routes (index, paginate, new,
create, show, edit, update, destroy) in the order the Router needs,
with "new" and "page/{page}" before "{id}". Route::prefix groups
routes under a URI prefix. config/routes.php uses Route::resource for
the admin events routes, keeping the same names, URIs and middlewares.
